  "sourceInfo": {
    "description": "The Companion Bible Notes",
    "language": "en",
    "detailed_info": "Ethelbert William Bullinger (1837–1913) was an English clergyman, biblical scholar, and ultradispensationalist theologian known for his extraordinary linguistic abilities and meticulous attention to the structures of Scripture. His Companion Bible Notes, published between 1909 and 1922, contain detailed marginal notes, appendices, and textual observations covering the entire Bible, with special attention to figures of speech, Hebrew and Greek word studies, and the internal structure of the biblical text.\n\nPublic domain. Prepared by SermonIndex.net — https://www.sermonindex.net/commentary/cbnotes/",
    "history_of_changes": "(2026-09-27) Published by SermonIndex.net"
  },
